# Note: do NOT ignore **/README.md — apps/api/pyproject.toml's `readme = "README.md"`
# requires the file inside the build context.
docs/
# …except the one file a build actually reads. apps/merchant renders its API
# reference from the published contract at build time (contract.ts), so with
# `docs/` excluded wholesale `next build` died on ENOENT inside the image while
# building fine on a developer's machine, where the file is simply there.
# BuildKit honours a re-include under an excluded directory; keep it to the one
# file so the rest of docs/ stays out of every context.
!docs/api/merchant-openapi.json
e2e/
playwright-report/
test-results/
